== Modelling choices (where the GDDs leave the model a reading) ==
  M1 Seed contexts hold the 15 axis-seed rows' flags only (rev 12): modifier and timing rows are not read by lock_pass (it matches a row by (flag, pushes)) or load_check (except D15, which play cannot reach because set_story_flag clears the group). The three Aldric-kill flags and the three Seraphina command-hall flags are branches of one choice each but no exclusive group, so the contexts are a superset of what play sets. Seeds are fixed before C8-S13 (Act 1); side-arc flags join after Y2-PP-T17 maps them (AC15) and are not modelled. Walks use the rev 12 seed map for every reading; the earlier texts' seed maps are read only by the unit tables.
  M2 Contexts are walked once per lock_pass signature: the transitions read seeds only through lock_pass.
  M3 A save is any reachable state outside the four suppression windows, plus every checkpoint. A quit or crash reloads an earlier save, which is a reachable state already in the walk, so reload edges add no states; A1/A2 check every save's load.
  M4 The `world_map` path is modelled only for re-entry (after leaving Root of Heaven, and from Story+); before the Chapter 9 end Root of Heaven is not on the map (lifecycle S6).
  M5 Positions are coarse: Chapter 9 is one position; the boss is one event (ROOT -> final authorization). A crisis-time save would sit at S16_OPEN.
  M6 D14 'matching' = the beat id retract_<rule of the row before the renegotiation>_<axis>_<new>, now stated in Edge Case 16 (rev 10); D1's four clauses are tagged in the order secret, UNSET axis, invalid row, other ID.
  M7 In 1.0 the invocation input I is always false (no source exists); every knob is false. Knob values are read only by formula_id at C8-S16 and the gate, so A6 also covers a mid-play knob patch.
  M8 Story+ (after T9) offers no route back to the boss or the final authorization; re-entering Root of Heaven from Story+ is T8 only. Whether Story+ can replay the boss belongs to the combat system (lifecycle Open Question 2).
  M9 The accepted-record probe applies one field change to every reachable save (both readings' saves are the same); 'accepted' means load_check is empty and no play in the mutated seed signature writes that (record, position). The D7 new-value fixture is the one two-field edit (the entry's `new` and its beat).
  M10 A live DAMAGED record at the gate is TURNED_BACK by the gate's DAMAGED row and is not a transition (kind GATE_DAMAGED); the walk never produces one (A8), so L-AC8's cells inject it.
  M11 'Inside C8-S16 before its commit' is the position S16_OPEN (rev 11, live_crisis).
  M12 D0 (rev 12) is modelled as far as a typed record can express it: an axis, root_phase or retraction enum outside its values, an element of the wrong type, retraction_log over one entry, beats_played over sixteen (rev 12) or one (rev 13); a missing field through decode() of a current-schema save. 'A set holding one element twice' is NOT modelled: a frozenset cannot hold one, so that D0 fixture belongs to SaveService's decoder tests. D0 checks only that beats_played elements are strings; which beat ids exist is D14's (Edge Case 16).
  M13 A save of the schema version before the lifecycle fields has no lifecycle block; decode() fills it with EMPTY before load_check (Edge Case 8); rev 13 derives its position from its scene (LEGACY_SCENES stands in for the scene-to-id map). Chapter select writes its record at CH9 as the walk's second start, and rev 13 adds 'Chapter 8 - Ending' at S16_DONE as a third (CHAPTER_SELECT_ENTRIES stands in for main_menu.gd).
  M15 NG+ is a unit check, not a walk edge: an NG+ edge would start a new record and so trip A6 (a stored ID never changes), which holds within one cycle. The unit starts a new cycle from every position after the final authorization.
  M14 Kaelthas is outside the 1.0 companion set (Core Rule 11); the model never modelled companions, and the ch3_kaelthas_* exclusive group stays because it is game code that D15 reads.
  M16 Rev 14 covers the whole stored record at the save level (stored_save_check): the lifecycle block plus act1_pace, story_position, companions_present (the three 1.0 companions) and timing_flags (the six timing flags), each against its allowed values. The walk's Record stays the lifecycle block with the position beside it. regions_completed is not modelled (the GDD gives 'ids of the eight regions', no enumerated list) and the act2-4 paces wait for S06b's names; derived fields (storyline_phase, secret_route, family) are never stored. SCENE_TO_ID and HUB_SCENES stand in for Y1-P1-T03's scene-to-id map (story scenes only) and the game's hubs. load_check_tags keeps reporting D0 as one item for every text; d0_clauses gives rev 14's clause ids.

